    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm trying to refine our reorder logic for some lithium-ion battery cells we get from Shenzhen. We keep hitting stockouts during peak season because our lead times are pretty unpredictable. Can you help me draft a formula or some basic logic for calculating safety stock so we don't run dry while waiting for shipments?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard approach is to calculate safety stock using a formula that factors in desired service level and demand variability. Start by determining your average daily demand and the standard deviation of demand during your lead time. You can then use the formula: $Safety\\ Stock = Z \\times \\sigma_{L}$, where $Z$ is the Z-score for your target service level and $\\sigma_{L}$ is the standard deviation of demand during lead time. This helps absorb unexpected spikes and shipping delays.",
      "source": "target",
