      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When lead time itself is highly variable, you need to incorporate both demand uncertainty and lead time uncertainty into your safety stock calculation. A more robust method involves calculating the standard deviation of demand over the *maximum possible* lead time, or using a simulation approach. Essentially, increase the volatility factor ($Z$) significantly, or model the uncertainty in the lead time itself to create a more conservative buffer against unpredictable disruptions.",
      "source": "target",
